{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "11", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "00", "M": "16", "S": "21"}}, "news": [{"title": "NLMC issues RFP to e-auction 11 government residential flats in Prayagraj", "para": "The National Land Monetization Corporation has unveiled a Request for Proposal for the auctioning of residential flats situated in three housing schemes throughout Prayagraj, Uttar Pradesh. The e-auction is set for December 11, following a pre-bid meeting on November 20. Those interested in participating should register and provide the Earnest Money Deposit by December 7. Further bidding details can be found on the specified e-auction portal.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/nlmc-issues-rfp-to-e-auction-11-government-residential-flats-in-prayagraj/135710954?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-302142/135710954.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Consumer panel directs Bombay Realty to  refund \u20b91.95 crore to two homebuyers", "para": "In a significant ruling, the Maharashtra Consumer Commission has ordered Bombay Dyeing and Bombay Realty to reimburse homebuyers a total of Rs 1.95 crore. The commission noted that the developers did not meet the agreed-upon deadlines for flat delivery, highlighting a breach of service. Homebuyers from Jamshedpur encountered both delays and unreasonable financial requests.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/consumer-panel-directs-bombay-realty-to-refund-1-95-crore-to-two-homebuyers/135710463?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-91530/135710463.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Quick-commerce sector may require 75 million sq ft urban logistics space by 2030: Report", "para": "By 2030, India's quick-commerce sector is predicted to require around 75 million sq ft of urban logistics space. The expansion of dark stores is rapidly reaching tier-II and tier-III cities, indicating a significant growth in warehousing demand. As operators pursue partner-led models for optimization, this evolution will transform urban logistics landscape in India. It marks a critical shift in meeting the expanding needs of the market.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/quick-commerce-sector-may-require-75-million-sq-ft-urban-logistics-space-by-2030-report/135699177?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-257698/135699177.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}]}